Lavaan group -

I'm trying to specify the model attached in the picture where Constituents Attitudes is the exogenous variable and all others are endogenous. The relationship between the exogenous variable Constituents Attitudes and Congressmen Perceptions is 1, which seems wrong. I have what I think is a correlation, but might be a covariance matrix:

library(lavaan)

library(semPlot)

lower <- matrix(c(1, NA, NA, NA, .475, 1, NA, NA, .738, .643, 1, NA, .608, .721, .823, 1), 4, 4, byrow = TRUE)

colnames(lower) <- rownames(lower) <- c("consAtt", "congressAtt", "perceptions", "rollCallBehav")

mod1 <- '

# latent vars

consAtt =~ perceptions

# regressions

congressAtt ~ perceptions

rollCallBehav ~ perceptions + congressAtt

'

mod1fit <- sem(mod1, sample.cov = lower, sample.nobs = 116)

semPaths(mod1fit, what = "est", layout = "tree2", title = TRUE, style = "LISREL", nCharNodes = 10)

